    "relations": "is-a edges (parents) drive KAMEL valid-ancestor traversal; treats edges link a procedure/device/drug to the conditions it is indicated for and are used only to connect a claimed diagnosis to procedure-centric policy or evidence text.",
    "description": "Curated knowledge graph for the NCD 80.x (Eye) research corpus: a subset of ICD-10-CM diagnosis codes plus project-defined grouping, finding, procedure, device and drug concepts, with is-a edges used for KAMEL-style valid-ancestor traversal.",
    "icd10cm_source": "ICD-10-CM code titles are U.S. government works published by CMS/CDC (NCHS) and are in the public domain; only the codes needed by this research corpus are included, with titles abbreviated in a few places. Laterality/7th-character extensions are omitted.",
    "non_icd_concepts": "Concepts whose system is GROUP, FINDING, PROC, DEVICE or DRUG are project-authored research constructs (not an official terminology) used to connect policy language to ICD-10-CM codes. Synonyms are hand-curated.",
    "va_eligible_note": "Chapter/block/system roots are marked va_eligible=false: they are too generic to be KAMEL valid ancestors (a 'disorder of the eye' must not satisfy a policy condition about a specific disease)."
  },
